but I'm just kind of using my materials that I already use.

2
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.800
So, let's talk about automotive cybersecurity, right?

3
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.800
I'm sure all of you are familiar with the concept of a car

4
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.800
and what a car's original intended purpose is, right?

5
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.800
The idea is that a vehicle is something you can sit inside

6
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.800
and it will take you very quickly from point A to point B.

7
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.800
So, traditionally, the most important features of a vehicle

8
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.800
are its ability to transport you from one area to another

9
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.800
safely, quickly, and comfortably, right?

10
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.800
But as automotive technology got more advanced,

11
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.800
we began to introduce different technological advances

12
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.800
into these vehicles, right?

13
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.800
Modern car from the late 1990s, early 2000s, 2010s

14
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.800
has a lot of technology for just making your driver experience more pleasant.

15
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.800
You have things like GPS, you have navigation,

16
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.800
you have the ability to stream music from your cell phone, right?

17
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.800
You can pair your cell phone to your car over Bluetooth

18
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.800
and you can play the music from your phone on Spotify or YouTube or whatever.

19
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.800
It doesn't matter.

20
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.800
At the same time, the actual internal vehicle electronics

21
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.800
also got a lot more technologically advanced.

22
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.800
They became more efficient and they became lighter, right?

23
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.800
The introduction of vehicle networking technologies, right?

24
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.800
Special networking technologies that are used inside vehicles

25
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.800
allowed the manufacturers to save a ton of money

26
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.800
on the actual copper used for wiring

27
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.800
because instead of having point-to-point-to-point

28
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.800
fully populated mesh networks of all the different microcontrollers

29
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.800
inside the car, they could use a bus network topology

30
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:30.800
and cut down like maybe 70, 80% of the wiring

31
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.800
they needed to put inside the vehicle,

32
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.800
which made the vehicles lighter, which made them cheaper,

33
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.800
and made them more reliable as these kinds of networking technologies got advanced.

34
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.800
And then now if you look at the modern car,

35
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.900
you see that we're adding things like cameras,

36
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.900
we're adding things like LiDAR sensors,

37
00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.900
long-range cellular networking technology, right?

38
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.900
Wi-Fi, the ability to run a Wi-Fi hotspot from inside your car.

39
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.900
I actually don't own a car here in Japan, funnily enough.

40
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:54.900
I just don't really need one.

41
