77
00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.900
So you'll have several ECUs inside your powertrain system

78
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.900
that are responsible for actually moving the car,

79
00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.900
the throttle, the braking, the steering, etc.

80
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.900
Yes.

81
00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.900
ECUs and other parts, yeah.

82
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:42.900
Yes.

83
00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:43.900
Any questions?

84
00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:44.900
No, no, no.

85
00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:45.900
No, no, no, sorry.

86
00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.900
Yeah, you could even tweak the configuration of the engine,

87
00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.900
so you can do everything with the ECU.

88
00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.900
That's cool.

89
00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:52.900
Exactly, yeah.

90
00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.900
And so a lot of that intelligence inside the vehicle

91
00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.900
is concentrated around these ECUs and their ability

92
00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.900
to carry out the different functions inside the car.

93
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.900
And when these began to be implemented inside vehicles

94
00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.900
and used where software was really defining

95
00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.000
what a vehicle could do,
